# Related Navigation

Related navigation links to useful adjacent content. It complements the current task without becoming a second site map. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/related-navigation/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a small set of meaningful links after a device guide or beside a long documentation article. Examples include installation requirements beside a theme-settings page, or a device manual beside a maintenance record. Order by user need, not by an assumed popularity score.

## Structure and behaviour

Mark the group as navigation and give it a specific label such as "More about theme installation". Use concise destination titles. On narrow screens, move related links after the main content in the same reading order. Explain external destinations when leaving HA or the documentation.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not infer household relationships, expose hidden dashboards or recommend external services. Only link to destinations the current user may access. Do not copy government organisation, world-location or policy classifications into the household interface.

